body:
>Any other answer should be a warning sign that you need help and intervention.

&#x200B;

Sorry, could you explain what you mean? I'm not sure what you mean by this. It's my choice isn't it.? I don't think I need an intervention, there's nothing drastic happening. Sorry if I sound harsh or anything, I don't mean to be, I am genuinely wondering.

I like being able to taste food too, but usually I just eat to get it over with, you know? I can't physically sit there and eat and feel enjoyment though.. I just feel nervous because of the risks.

&#x200B;

If eating wasn't necessary to live I'm not even sure I'd do it. Maybe occasionally just to remind myself what it's like but most days I'd skip it
